12	/// The chat feature's one remote data source — non-streaming calls go
13	/// through `ApiClient`'s plain JSON methods exactly like
14	/// `EntriesRemoteDataSource`'s own `create`/`list`/`get`; [sendMessage]/
15	/// [retryMessage] alone go through `ApiClient.postStream`, sharing the one
16	/// piece of SSE-specific logic this story introduces (`_consumeSse`):
17	/// splitting the raw byte stream into `event:`/`data:` blocks and mapping
18	/// each into a [ChatStreamEvent] (or an in-band [Failure]) — kept
19	/// feature-local per the Code Map, `ApiClient` itself knows nothing about
20	/// the SSE grammar.
21	class ChatRemoteDataSource {
22	  ChatRemoteDataSource(this._apiClient);
